1. New option for left-handed players, can be chosen in the main menu;

2. Graphics optimizations for some background and objects.


Since boss fights could be hard to access for many players, we managed to add a new training boss level separatly for each stage, will apply soon in next patch:)

At first we’d planed to update the demo weekly, however there were too many changes we added to the game, just have to make sure all is great:). 

The gameplay of this version is very much close to Early Access of Revoke, though we are still doing new experiments in it~

Details:
1. Three new elite enemies added; All enemy AI logic rebuilt, now they move slower and have less HP, but more dangerous;

2. Health packs no longer lying in the map, they’ll drop from specific enemies, you need to shoot them to get healed;

3. P90 like gun comes back as an additional weapon;

So I think the game experience could be more arcady than before, meanwhile challenge degree stays the same, hope you like it.

This weekend we just find out that our VR gamers' shooting skill is far beyond our expectation :). So we discussed about every feedback collected and worked out this first new version.

1. Demo difficulty is REMARKABLY HIGHER than before. We increased both enemy AI and fire rates, so it could be more challenging and needs strategies to win.
To balance that, we‘ll also make skills other than "time freezing“ more powerful and essential to use in  the coming updates;

2. The "Start" button can be accurately aimed with Vive controllers now; 

3. P90 like gun is temporarily replaced by a new pistol, we improved the whole shooting experience and added some shooting feedback to the enemies. (We're still working on a new and much better enemy-getting-hit action, will apply soon) Hope you'd like it;

4. We adjusted the effect of time freezing skill, it becomes less bright and more comfortable when using it;

5. We change "snap turn" to a "smooth turn" for Rift users;  

We'll be working overtime this week and try to update the demo again by weekend, any feedbacks is always welcome, thanks! 


Cheers,
Ke
